But that leaves you with a question. It is a little weird for you to be sitting on the beanbag while <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> takes the floor, <span style="color:Yelllow">so you have to choose between lying on the ground next to him, maybe closer than the beanbags allow, or perhaps using something else as your seat.</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
    <<link "Cuddle next to Carter<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        You follow suit, moving your beanbag aside and lying down right next to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, <span style="color:LightGreen">so close that your bodies are touching.</span> The boy laughs at this. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You didn’t have to move to the floor too.”</span> Though you tell him that he made it look comfortable and place one of your arms over his shoulder. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> chuckles at this and does the same thing with his arm. <span style="color:LightGreen">This leaves you both lying there, one hand on each other as the other hand supports your head as you glance up at cartoons. <br>
        <br>
